From: openwrt-xiaomi-ax3000t-rd03v2 port
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: compensate the management frame signal on IPQ5018+QCN6122

The WLAN.HK.2.7.0.1 firmware used with the multi-PD IPQ5018+QCN6122
combination reports the SNR of received management frames on an
uncalibrated scale: v1.x measured scan results ~31 dB (2.4 GHz) / ~24 dB
(5 GHz) below the level an independent receiver reads for the same
beacons. Add those offsets where the WMI mgmt rx event is converted to
dBm, which is what scan results and the probe request signal that
hostapd and steering daemons see come from.

This is the management-frame half of the v1.x port's 952. Its station
signal offsets are not carried: with NSS Wi-Fi offload the station signal
is already reported in dBm.

CANDIDATE: not applied. Moves into v2/overlay only if phase C (C5) shows
this tree's scan results reading low against an independent receiver.
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.h
@@ -1514,4 +1514,22 @@ static inline struct ath11k_peer *ath11k_peer_find_by_id(struct ath11k *ar,
 	return peer;
 }
 
+/* WLAN.HK.2.7.0.1 on IPQ5018/QCN6122 reports the SNR of received management
+ * frames on an uncalibrated scale (measured ~31 dB low on 2.4 GHz, ~24 dB low
+ * on 5 GHz against external references). Compensate where the WMI mgmt rx
+ * event is converted to dBm. Station signal with NSS Wi-Fi offload is already
+ * in dBm and is not touched.
+ */
+static inline s8 ath11k_hw_mgmt_rssi_offset(struct ath11k_base *ab)
+{
+	switch (ab->hw_rev) {
+	case ATH11K_HW_IPQ5018_HW10:
+		return 31;
+	case ATH11K_HW_QCN6122_HW10:
+		return 24;
+	default:
+		return 0;
+	}
+}
+
 #endif /* _CORE_H_ */
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/wmi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/wmi.c
@@ -7865,7 +7865,8 @@ static void ath11k_mgmt_rx_event(struct ath11k_base *ab, struct sk_buff *skb)
 		status->freq = ieee80211_channel_to_frequency(rx_ev.channel,
 							      status->band);
 
-	status->signal = rx_ev.snr + ATH11K_DEFAULT_NOISE_FLOOR;
+	status->signal = rx_ev.snr + ATH11K_DEFAULT_NOISE_FLOOR +
+			 ath11k_hw_mgmt_rssi_offset(ab);
 	status->rate_idx = ath11k_mac_bitrate_to_idx(sband, rx_ev.rate / 100);
 
 	hdr = (struct ieee80211_hdr *)skb->data;
